  Author: "sliptonic"
  License: "CC-BY-SA-4.0"
  Name: "Steel 1018"
  Description: >-
    AISI 1018 low-carbon (mild) steel, cold-drawn condition. One of the most
    common general-purpose carbon steels for machining.
    Density and Young's modulus: Wikipedia article "Carbon steel" (CC-BY-SA-4.0),
    accessed 2026-05.
    Yield/ultimate strengths: typical published values for 1018 cold-drawn
    at room temperature.
    Thermal properties (k, c_p, α): typical values for low-carbon steel
    (widely-published engineering data).
    Machinability data derived from FreeCAD core 'MildSteel.FCMat' (Jonas Bähr,
    CC-BY-3.0, sourced from Tabellenbuch Zerspantechnik ISBN 978-3-7585-1315-2).
    Original Jonas Bähr k_c1.1 base value (1800 N/mm^2) reads slightly low
    for 0.18% C steel (Kienzle reference for C20 is ~1990 N/mm^2); the
    Jonas-corrected milling value of 2298 N/mm^2 is retained as a reasonable
    central estimate. Hot-rolled 1018 has lower yield (~220-310 MPa) than the
    cold-drawn values shown here.
  SourceURL: "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_steel"
  Tags:
    - "Steel"
    - "1018"
    - "Mild Steel"
    - "Low Carbon"
    - "Cold Drawn"
    - "UNS G10180"
    - "AISI 1018"
